In the bustling emergency room, triage nurses swiftly scanned the health cards;
to ensure no critical case was overlooked, she checked every name aloud before the team could whisk patients away,
despite the curtained section where monitors beeped urgently.
Amidst the flurry, a doctor scribbled prescriptions; amidst the chaos,
he moved deftly between each bay where IVs dripped steadily for the weary.
The corridor echoed with whispered concerns from anxious companions;
while behind the counter, an intercom crackled with calls for urgent care,
a patient clutched their form tightly, fretting over the endless wait.
With charts fluttering in her hands, another nurse hurried past;
under the fluorescent lights, wristbands glowed brightly, marking time.

In the bustling heart of the ER, patients waited anxiously beside the gurneys; 
to be seen by a nurse, one must first fill out paperwork indicating their condition;
beside them, monitors beeped steadily, attached to those lying on stretchers;
the doctor, rushing from bay to bay, attended to each patient with utmost care;
though many complained about the long wait under the shadow of drawn curtains,
some understood the gravity of sorting through cases based on severity;
amidst the chaos, an intercom echoed urgent calls, guiding staff to specific rooms;
in one corner, a patient leaned heavily on a chair, surrounded by concerned faces;
behind the counter, wristbands were being printed and handed out efficiently;
as a nurse approached, she prepared to enter the patient’s details into the system.
